diff --git a/docs/consumer.rst b/docs/consumer.rst
index 59b84b7..49ef431 100644
--- a/docs/consumer.rst
+++ b/docs/consumer.rst
@@ -480,3 +480,56 @@ Signals
 The consumer will emit certain :ref:`signals` as it executes tasks. User code
 can register signal handlers to respond to these events. For more information,
 see the :ref:`signals` document.
+
+Leased SQLite delivery
+----------------------
+
+``LeasedSqliteHuey`` opts into durable message reservations. Configure all
+consumers for a queue with this class; a normal SQLite consumer removes messages
+without acknowledging them and must not share that queue::
+
+    from huey import LeasedSqliteHuey
+
+    huey = LeasedSqliteHuey('jobs', filename='jobs.db', lease_seconds=60)
+
+    @huey.task(context=True)
+    def process_chunks(chunks, task=None):
+        for chunk in chunks:
+            process(chunk)
+            if not task.renew_lease():
+                return  # Ownership expired; another attempt may already run.
+
+Both thread and process consumers reserve work through the normal dequeue path.
+An unacknowledged message becomes available when its lease expires, including
+after an uncatchable worker termination. ``lease_seconds`` must be positive and
+finite. An optional ``clock`` callable supplies Unix seconds for leases; it does
+not replace Huey's task ETA clock. Applications using a custom clock must keep
+it consistent across processes.
+
+``task.lease_token`` identifies the current reservation generation, not the
+logical task. ``task.renew_lease(now=None)`` returns whether renewal succeeded.
+A normal task or immediate-mode invocation has no lease token and cannot renew.
+An expired attempt raises ``LeaseLost`` before execution or while completing;
+it cannot acknowledge a new owner's work. There is no automatic heartbeat.
+
+The storage exposes ``reserve``, ``owns``, ``ack``, ``release``, ``renew`` and
+``inflight_count``. All accept optional Unix ``now`` values; omitted values use
+the configured clock. Reservations expose ``token``, ``data``, and ``expires_at``.
+An expiry equal to the current time is expired. Queue counts and inspection
+show only available work; in-flight counts show active reservations. Flushing
+a queue removes its reservations as well as its pending messages.
+
+User task bodies run outside a database write transaction. Huey's completion
+writes (results, successor messages, retries and acknowledgement) commit
+together. ``enqueue_due()`` similarly moves due scheduled messages atomically;
+the normal scheduler calls it automatically. Failed completion or promotion
+transactions leave the original work recoverable. Result/signal hooks still
+execute application code; their external effects cannot be rolled back.
+
+This is at-least-once delivery. A task whose lease expires while it runs may be
+executed again. Make external effects safe to repeat and size or renew leases
+appropriately. Immediate execution is unchanged. Invalid serialized messages
+are discarded and logged as in ordinary Huey. The feature does not add a
+general exactly-once protocol to groups/chords or extend SQLite's own durability
+guarantees. Existing database files and explicit ``initialize_schema()`` are
+supported; ``create_tables=False`` performs no automatic schema creation.
